    {
      "path": "dsh-bundle.yml",
      "text": "# Repo-root bundle layer for the ENGINE repository installed as a DSH bundle (`dsh plugin add\n# github:Johnly1986/AmberFlow`, git+file, tarball). This is the git-install door: pnpm clones the\n# whole repository, so the plugin entry is addressed as a subpath of the installed package — the\n# form the publish guide shows (`dsh-hello-plugin/startup`) — and Node resolution finds the module.\n#\n# No config and no build script by design: the package-root \".\" export points at the plugin's\n# TypeScript source, which the harness loads under its own TS runtime, so `dsh plugin add <git>`\n# needs no allowBuilds grant; the bridge locates the checkout it ships inside (or AMBERFLOW_REPO /\n# a config override). The nested package keeps its own cordis.patch.yml for link/path installs of\n# `integrations/dsh-bridge`.\n#\n# The row names the PACKAGE ROOT (`amberflow`), not a subpath: the DSH client-module scanner only\n# serves a browser half for a package-root row, and the configuration page needs that scanner to\n# find this package's `dsh.client`. `amberflow/dsh-plugin` remains a compatible export alias for\n# older hand-written profile patches.\n- insert:\n    - id: amberflow-bridge\n      name: amberflow\n"
    }
  ],
